{
  "title": "Extract action-choice handling from BridgeCallbackHandler.java",
  "description": "After extracting prompt formatting, view lookup, oracle lookup, state building, and game-log formatting, `BridgeCallbackHandler.java` is down to 5253 lines but still has a very large decision-surface chunk. `buildActionChoices()` starts around line 839, `chooseAction()` around line 1884, and the batch combat helpers live around lines 2576 and 2701.\n\nThat remaining area still mixes several responsibilities:\n- building MCP-facing choice payloads for `GAME_SELECT`, `GAME_TARGET`, `GAME_CHOOSE_*`, amount prompts, and pile choices\n- validating/decoding model responses back into XMage responses\n- combat-specific choice rendering and batch attacker/blocker execution\n- stale-choice tracking and default-action coordination\n\nSuggested split:\n1. `ActionChoicesBuilder` for read-only choice payload construction\n2. `ChooseActionExecutor` for response decoding/validation and response delivery\n3. `BatchCombatHandler` for attacker/blocker parsing and execution\n\nKeeping those concerns together makes the bridge decision boundary harder to reason about and harder to test in isolation.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "bridge",
    "refactoring",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-03-21T00:02:18.900310-07:00",
